## Question 1: Why Portfolio on Netlify, JobTrack on InfinityFree?

| Feature | Netlify | InfinityFree |
|---------|---------|--------------|
| **Best for** | Static sites (HTML/CSS/JS/React) | Dynamic sites (PHP + MySQL) |
| **Backend support** | ❌ No PHP, No MySQL | ✅ PHP, MySQL, Databases |
| **File uploads** | ❌ Limited | ✅ Yes |
| **Email sending** | Via EmailJS (3rd party) | Via PHP SMTP |
| **React support** | ✅ Perfect | ⚠️ Needs configuration |
| **Free SSL** | ✅ Auto | ✅ Manual |
| **Build time** | Instant | N/A |

### Why Portfolio on Netlify?
- Your portfolio is **React (static)** - no database, no PHP
- Netlify is **built for React** → faster, simpler, free SSL
- InfinityFree doesn't easily support React routing

### Why JobTrack Pro on InfinityFree?
- JobTrack needs **PHP + MySQL** (backend logic, database)
- Netlify **cannot run PHP** at all
- InfinityFree is perfect for PHP/MySQL apps

### Summary:
```
Static React Site → Netlify (free, fast, simple)
PHP + MySQL App → InfinityFree (supports backend)
```

